<!doctype html>
{%- comment -%}
  LOCAL OVERRIDE of al_folio_core's _layouts/default.liquid (copied verbatim from
  gem 1.0.15).

  ONE change from the gem's version: the `page.noindex` block inside <head> below.

  Why this file and not _includes/head.liquid: a `<meta name="robots">` only counts
  if it is inside <head>, and the gem offers no hook there — `hook/bib.liquid`, used
  by _layouts/bib.liquid, is the ONLY hook in the whole gem. (An earlier attempt put
  the tag in `_includes/hook/head.liquid`; the gem never calls it, so it silently did
  nothing. Verified live before this file existed.) That leaves overriding one of the
  two templates that build <head>. This one is 87 lines and is mostly the stable
  page skeleton; head.liquid is 208 lines of conditional asset includes that shift
  with every theme feature, so it is much the worse thing to pin a copy of.

  After `bundle update` of al_folio_core, compare against the gem's version with:
    bundle exec al-folio upgrade overrides diff _layouts/default.liquid
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  al_rtl owns the language and direction attributes when it is installed, because
  `dir` has to sit on <html> for the browser's bidi handling, CSS logical
  properties and Tailwind's rtl: variant to apply to the whole document.

  Captured into a variable rather than wrapping the <html> tag in a conditional:
  a conditional there stops the tag being a single static element, and Prettier
  then re-indents the entire document body. The guard keeps this parse-safe —
  without the plugin the tag does not exist and Liquid fails on every page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture html_attributes -%}
  {%- if site.plugins contains 'al_rtl' -%}
    {%- include plugins/al_rtl_html_attrs.liquid -%}
  {%- else -%}
    lang="{{ site.lang }}"
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
<html {{ html_attributes }}>
  <!-- Head -->
  <head>
    {% if page.redirect %}
      {% if page.redirect == true %}
        {% assign redirect = site.baseurl | append: '/' %}
      {% elsif page.redirect contains '://' %}
        {% assign redirect = page.redirect %}
      {% else %}
        {% assign redirect = page.redirect | relative_url %}
      {% endif %}
      <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="3; url={{ redirect }}">
    {% endif %}
    {%- comment -%}
      LOCAL CHANGE (see the note at the top of this file). A page with

        noindex: true

      in its front matter asks search engines not to index it. Together with
      `nav: false` and `sitemap: false` this is the unlisted-page pattern in
      CLAUDE.md §8 — see _pages/talks.md, the one page using it.

      This is obscurity, not access control: the repository is public, so the URL
      is readable in the repo whatever this tag says. It stops the page turning up
      in a search; it does not stop anyone who has the address.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% if page.noindex %}
      <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
    {% endif %}
    {% include head.liquid %}
  </head>

  <!-- Body -->
  <body class="{% if site.navbar_fixed %}fixed-top-nav{% endif %} {% unless site.footer_fixed %}sticky-bottom-footer{% endunless %}">
    <!-- Header -->
    {% include header.liquid %}

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="container mt-5" role="main">
      {% if page.toc and page.toc.sidebar %}
        {% assign toc_collapse = page.toc.collapse | default: 'expanded' %}
        {% assign toc_collapse_depth = page.toc.collapse_depth | default: '' %}
        {% if page.toc.sidebar == 'right' %}
          <div class="row">
            <!-- main content area -->
            <div class="col-sm-9">{{ content }}</div>
            <!-- sidebar, which will move to the top on a small screen -->
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <nav
                id="toc-sidebar"
                class="sticky-top toc toc-sidebar"
                aria-label="Table of contents"
                data-toc-collapse="{{ toc_collapse }}"
                data-toc-collapse-depth="{{ toc_collapse_depth }}"
              ></nav>
            </div>
          </div>
        {% else %}
          <div class="row">
            <!-- sidebar, which will move to the top on a small screen -->
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <nav
                id="toc-sidebar"
                class="sticky-top toc toc-sidebar"
                aria-label="Table of contents"
                data-toc-collapse="{{ toc_collapse }}"
                data-toc-collapse-depth="{{ toc_collapse_depth }}"
              ></nav>
            </div>
            <!-- main content area -->
            <div class="col-sm-9">{{ content }}</div>
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      {% else %}
        {{ content }}
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <!-- Footer -->
    {% include footer.liquid %}

    <!-- JavaScripts -->
    {% include scripts.liquid %}
  </body>
</html>
